{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"certifiable":true,"criteria":[{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":150,"line_start":145,"path":"README.md"},"criterion":"The Jira extras' documentation names `acli` as a required external binary for the Cloud path, with an install pointer, and states that the Data Center path does not need it. (README.md prerequisite bullet, docs/jira-sync-setup.md non-container note, pyproject.toml `[jira-datacenter]`-exempt comment)","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":200,"line_start":178,"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py"},"criterion":"A missing `acli` produces a typed, actionable failure naming the binary and the remedy — not a bare `[Errno 2]`. (`AcliNotInstalledError` raised at the `_run_acli` Popen site / `require_acli` preflight, message names `acli`, Cloud, and docs/jira-sync-setup.md; subclasses `FileNotFoundError` so existing handlers still catch it.)","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":130,"line_start":112,"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_acli_preflight_missing_binary.py"},"criterion":"The typed failure is distinguishable from `missing_credentials` and `missing_project`, so a caller can tell 'not installed' from 'not configured'. (Held-out test `test_missing_binary_vs_missing_credentials_are_distinct` proves the three states yield three distinct results.)","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":148,"line_start":133,"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_acli_preflight_missing_binary.py"},"criterion":"The Data Center path is demonstrably unaffected — it must not acquire a dependency on `acli`. (`test_data_center_path_d